Patch crosvm: goldfish battery fed by the host (mship.battery).

crosvm's goldfish battery gets live values only from a power monitor, and the only monitor upstream is
ChromeOS powerd (D-Bus). This adds the `mship` monitor: it reads the battery state that mship-battery
publishes on /run/mothership/battery.sock (MSHIP_BATTERY_SOCK overrides) and reconnects when the service
restarts. It also passes temperature, health and the FULL status to the guest. Upstream crosvm reports
temperature as 0, health as unknown and maps FULL to NOT_CHARGING.

